vention for HIV/AIDS prevention in sub-Saharan Africa</article-title><source>Soc Sci Med</source><year>2001</year><volume>53</volume><fpage>1397</fpage><lpage>1411</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11710416</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0277-9536(00)00427-5</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sweat</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Gregorich</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Sangiwa</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Furlonge</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Balmer</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Kamenga</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Grinstead</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Coates</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cost-effectiveness of voluntary HIV-1 counselling and testing in reducing sexual transmission of HIV-1 in Kenya and Tanzania</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>2000</year><volume>356</volume><fpage>113</fpage><lpage>121</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10963247</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0140-6736(00)02447-8</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Colebunders</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Ndumbe</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Priorities for HIV testing in developing countries?</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>1993</year><volume>342</volume><fpage>601</fpage><lpage>602</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8102727</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0140-6736(93)91417-K</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Grinstead</surname><given-names>OA</given